    "tree_id": "87ba24ff20c206194f254c073873f2f6c7f2573c",
    "message": "feat(http): share cleartext listeners between H1 and prior-knowledge H2\n\nNative HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 prior-knowledge clients can share one\ncleartext TCP listener using `transport: :tcp, protocols: [:http2,\n:http1], h2c: :prior_knowledge`. Embedded, standalone and Phoenix entry\npoints share the existing engines, listener and routing path; existing\nTCP defaults and TLS ALPN behavior are preserved.\n\nThe bounded pure classifier retains at most 23 undecided bytes and\nreplays every received byte exactly once after selection. Detection\nreuses the connection-owner admission lease, preserves drain identity\nand first-input deadlines, and allocates H2 resources only after\nselection and reservation. Absolute H2 startup checks prevent late\nSETTINGS acknowledgments from defeating an expired deadline.\nDocumentation, deterministic lifecycle regressions, real same-port\nH1/Python-h2 tests and standalone artifact smoke cover the new contract.\n\nValidation: independent specification/code/package review passed;\nfocused feature/configuration 47/47, ordinary exact-count gate 207/207,\nexisting body/H2/Plug/Phoenix/WebSocket compatibility 84/84, packaging\nharness 9/9, formatting and strict production compilation passed. The\n0.7.0 standalone smoke passed core 3 transports, gateway 7 exchanges (5\nmixed-port), and H3 3 checks. Raw logs and source/package receipts are\nin `docs/acceptance/evidence/mixed-h2c/`.\n\nAn unrelated existing H1-only low-budget upload failure at\n`http_network_test.exs:351` was reproduced on the baseline and remains\nexplicitly FAIL in `docs/acceptance/mixed-h2c.md`; assertions were\npreserved. Specialist pressure/soak/disconnect qualification remains\ndeferred. Publication uses the established coordinated\nfive-package/standalone workflow after hosted CI and main integration;\ndeployment is outside scope.",
